# CHANGES.log

## 2026-06-18 — Analyse workspace critical audit + reconciliation

Goal: terminate noise, keep only defensible signal; every feature must change a real
decision for the better. Methodology: Claude (architect) owned the audit + logic spec
+ review; Codex (executor) implemented the Scrap reframe + wrote the Vitest suite.
See docs/ANALYSE_PRD.md §0 (Goal & Methodology) and §1–§4 for equations/provenance.

Audit findings acted on:
- Scrap is DIFFUSE, not Pareto (32/94 products = 80%, top is ~9.7%) → killed the
  "vital few" framing; relabelled the concentration card; Pareto caption states the
  honest top-10 cumulative ("scrap is diffuse").
- The P25 "recoverable" was an arbitrary vanity number → replaced (see v2 below).
- Removed cosmetic driver() "likely lever" guesses.
- Scrap data relabelled line-level (Extrusion Line 1 / Machines 01 & 03), not MC01.
- Planner: false "Rate variability: measured from history" label → adjustable estimate
  (rateCv), wired through Monte-Carlo + levers. TOU made season-honest (summer/winter
  toggle; winter bands flat → lever only pays in summer). Default dataset → pilot (real).
- Delivery View reconciled to the system: MC01 single machine (was 3 + "add a machine"
  recommendation), 16 h/day, pilot/demo toggle defaulting to real.
- Dead code removed from productionModel.ts (planStrategy, planAll, buildSchedule,
  monteCarloFit, EPQ/MTS-MTO strategy engine).

Tests (Codex, src/lib/__tests__/productionModel.test.ts, Vitest): scheduleOrders
single-lane + priority-first + bounded steady-state + additive scrap; monteCarloOrders
bounded probs + sorted samples; scrap Pareto cumulative monotonic & first-80 index
(locks out the cumulative-line bug); recoverable excludes low-sample; dead exports
absent; source guards. Result: 6/6 pass. tsc clean. npm run build PROVENANCE CHECK PASSED.

## 2026-06-18 — Scrap Focus v2 (hard-pass follow-up)

Hard review of the live numbers found the gap-to-plant-average "recoverable" was
trivial (213 OMR/yr, 1.6% of loss) and hid the biggest, volume-driven losses
(PR110 #2 by scrap got zero recommendation because its rate was already below avg).

Fix (architect spec, Codex executed + tested):
- Per-product target -> each product's OWN best-demonstrated reject (its P25 across
  its own shift records; added as bestRejectOwn to scrapCatalog.json, null when <5
  records). Recoverable now 3,208 OMR/yr; top recs PR110 (~850) and DR152 (~810).
- Added a "Plant-wide lever" card: every 0.5 pp of line reject ~ 2,438 OMR/yr (1 pp
  ~ 4,876) — the honest headline for diffuse scrap. Replaced the Concentration card.
- Pareto + ranking now well-measured-only (24 of 94); banner states 5,472 OMR sits
  in 70 low-sample products excluded from ranking until more data.
- Table shows "Best %"; recs/drilldown read "reject X% -> your best Y% -> save Z".

Tests extended: recoverable uses bestRejectOwn & excludes null/low-sample; bestRejectOwn
non-null iff samples>=5; plant-wide sensitivity = 0.005*sum(demand*kg)*price; well-measured
Pareto cumulative monotonic & <=100. Result: 9/9 pass. tsc clean. build provenance passed.

## 2026-06-18 — Analyse journey: decision hub + scenario honesty + Validation Lab

Open-ended red-team (Codex) against the goal "simple journey -> confident decision"
surfaced: four analyst screens, no guided entry, generated orders shown as operational,
Plant Telemetry with no manager action. Founder decisions: scenario-mode (honest), one
"What do I do today?" hub as the entry, move Telemetry out of Analyse, keep demo toggles.

Implemented (architect spec, Codex executed + tested):
- New AnalyseHubPage = the Analyse landing. Two decision cards: "Will we ship on time?"
  (pAllOnTime% from the pilot order scenario, colour-coded, routes to Planner/Delivery)
  and "Where am I losing money to scrap?" (total scrap OMR + own-best recoverable, routes
  to Scrap Focus).
- ScenarioBanner (persistent, honest "generated order book, not live orders") on the hub,
  Planner, and Delivery. NOT on Scrap (real records) or Telemetry.
- Plant Telemetry moved OUT of Analyse into a top-level "Validation Lab" sidebar entry;
  Analyse children = Delivery, Planner, Scrap; Analyse parent opens the hub.
- Residual-bug fixes (architect): scrapCatalog.ts comment relabelled line-level; Scrap
  changeover card no longer contradicts the "diffuse" framing; changeover line says
  "on the line (MC01+03)".

Tests: 3 source guards added (Telemetry not an Analyse child + Validation Lab exists;
App has the analyse route + hub; ScenarioBanner text present on hub/Planner/Delivery and
absent from Scrap). Result: 12/12 pass. tsc clean. npm run build PROVENANCE CHECK PASSED.

## 2026-06-19 — Energy intensity (Planner) + Scrap diagnostic drill-down

Founder asked: make scrap recs prescriptive (where/why, not just "you have a problem"),
and add kWh/kg to the Planner. Data check: records have NO process settings
(temp/speed/vacuum/material lot), remarks_raw empty, color/class/wall constant per
product — so the ONLY within-product cause dimensions are shift (1 vs 2) and month.
The quantified "do Z -> cut X" engine is a DATA gap (process logging), not a hard model;
extrusion reject is process-empirical, not closed-form physics. Built the honest
diagnostic we CAN support today.

Architect data prep: added per-product shift1Reject, shift2Reject, monthly[] to
scrapCatalog.json (from shift1/2 scrap split + monthly aggregation) + types.

Implemented (Codex + tests):
- Planner: `energyIntensityKwhPerKg` helper; "kWh/kg" column in run-by-run detail;
  "Energy intensity — kWh per kg by product" bar chart (run energy only).
- Scrap drill-down "Where the loss is": shift-1 vs shift-2 reject with worse-shift
  callout (>=0.5pp); monthly trend sparkline (best vs worst month, capability-vs-
  consistency framing, bestRejectOwn marked); honest footer that exact-knob attribution
  needs run-level process logging.

Tests: 15/15 (energyIntensityKwhPerKg value+zero-guard; diagnostic fields present +
DU203 shift2>shift1 + monthly bounds; source guards). tsc clean; build provenance passed.

## 2026-06-19 — kWh/kg KPI on the decision hub (measured, line-level)

Founder wanted kWh/kg as a flagship KPI, benchmarked. Data check killed the per-product
version honestly: 0/94 products have a run rate, and there is NO per-machine/per-product
energy meter — only monthly whole-factory bills + MC01 production. Extruder specific energy
is also ~constant per material, so per-product variance is tiny; the real signal is
line×time utilization. Building 94 per-product kWh/kg would be fabrication.

Built instead (measured, honest): line×month kWh/kg from nizwa bills ÷ MC01 production
(energyKpi.json + energyKpi.ts). Range 1.14 (Mar-2026, best) .. 13.59 (Dec-2025, near-idle)
— electricity is ~fixed (~250-300k kWh/mo) so kWh/kg is a UTILIZATION metric. Added as the
3rd decision card on the Analyse hub: latest kWh/kg + best/worst benchmark + monthly
sparkline (best month highlighted) + driver caption + honest "factory bills, not yet
sub-metered" footnote. Per-product kWh/kg is now a headline data-request item.

Tests: 17/17 (energyKpi sanity: kwhPerKg>0, best=min, worst=max; hub source guard). tsc
clean; build provenance passed.
